  "database": "rschema_0147",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0147 database is designed to manage information about classes, members, announcements, messages, logs, and applications. The Class table stores details about each class, including its unique identifier, name, department name, and grade level. The Member table contains information about each member, such as their age, class affiliation, contact number, email, name, password, and workplace, with the Class_ID referencing the Class table to establish the relationship between a member and their class. The Announcement table stores announcements made to classes, including the announcement content, time, and the class it belongs to, with the Class_ID referencing the Class table to link the announcement to its class. The Message table stores messages sent between members, including the message content, read flag, send time, and the sender and receiver IDs, with the Receiver_ID and Sender_ID referencing the Member table to establish the sender and receiver relationships. The Log table stores logs of member activities, including the log content, member ID, mood, and time, with the Member_ID referencing the Member table to link the log to its member. The Application table stores applications submitted by members, including the application content, time, and approval flag, with the Member_ID referencing the Member table to establish the relationship between the application and its submitter.",
  "gold_question": "The key features of the system are as follows:\n1.Class Management: Manage class information, including class name, department name, grade, etc.\n2.Member Management: Manage the information of class members, including member ID, name, password, email, age, workplace, contact number, etc.\n3.Announcement Management: Publish and manage class announcements, including announcement ID, announcement time, and announcement content.\n4.Message Management: Manage class messages, allowing members to send messages. The system records sender ID, receiver ID, message content, send time, and read status.\n5.Log Management: Record class logs, including log ID, log content, time, mood, etc. Each member can post their own logs.\n6.Leave Management: Manage class messages, including message ID, message time, message content, and message count. Each member can leave messages.\n7.Application Management: Handle applications submitted by class members, including application ID, application time, approval status, and application content.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0147.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0147\nCREATE TABLE `class` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `grade_level` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `member` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `class_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `workplace` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `member_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`class_id`) REFERENCES `class` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `announcement` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `class_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `announcement_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`class_id`) REFERENCES `class` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `message` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `read_flag` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `send_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `sender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receiver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`receiver_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `log` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `mood` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `log_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `application` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `approval_flag` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `application_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
